Package: fosos-desktop
Version: 1.13.23
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3, python3-gi, python3-gi-cairo, python3-pamela, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-wnck-3.0, gir1.2-vte-2.91, gir1.2-lightdm-1, lightdm, python3-xlib, openbox, xss-lock, xcape, brightnessctl, brightness-udev, xsettingsd, arandr, scrot, x11-xkb-utils, x11-xserver-utils, network-manager, network-manager-gnome, blueman, gvfs, wireplumber, pipewire-bin, sound-theme-freedesktop, firmware-sof-signed, firmware-intel-sound, alsa-ucm-conf, locales, gnome-keyring, libpam-gnome-keyring, libsecret-1-0, fonts-inter, fonts-liberation, adwaita-icon-theme, pkexec, xdg-user-dirs, fosos-theme, fosos-cli
Recommends: freerdp3-x11, xrdp, xorgxrdp, pinentry-gnome3
Maintainer: FosOS <dev@fosos.local>
Description: FosOS Desktop session
 The FosOS panel, Start menu, desktop, Files, Terminal, Notepad,
 Remote Desktop client, notifications, lock screen, LightDM greeter and
 settings shell, running on the Openbox window manager. It is the default
 login session. A minimal FosOS Recovery session and text consoles are the
 fallback when the shell fails. Inbound RDP uses xrdp for a separate FosOS
 Desktop session (any local user); enable it from Settings → Remote Desktop.
